  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe proposed approach employs a Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) algorithm combined with a gradient-based local refinement. Unlike previous methods that relied on differential evolution or genetic algorithms, PSO offers a distinct exploration strategy that balances global search with local exploitation. By leveraging the inertia weight and social cognitive coefficients, we enable particles to explore diverse regions while gradually converging towards promising solutions. This hybrid method is expected to outperform earlier local search strategies by escaping local minima more effectively. The key improvement lies in the swarm's ability to maintain diversity, allowing for better exploration of the high-dimensional search space defined by the step function parameters.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: A step function h(x) \u2208 [0, 1] defined on [0, 2] with n_points samples, where h[i] \u2208 [0, 1] and \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2. The objective C\u2085 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx is evaluated using np.correlate with mode=\"full\", scaled by dx = 2.0 / n_points. The constraints are: \n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i (implicit through clipping)\n- \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2 (enforced by post-operation rescaling)\n\nPSO parameters:\n- Particle positions: h \u2208 [0,1]^n_points\n- Velocity: v \u2208 \u211d^n_points\n- Inertia weight: \u03c9 \u2208 [0.5, 1.5]\n- Cognitive coefficient: \u03b1 \u2208 [1.5, 2.5]\n- Social coefficient: \u03b2 \u2208 [1.5, 2.5]\n- Personal best position: pbest \u2208 [0,1]^n_points\n- Global best position: gbest \u2208 [0,1]^n_points\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nInput: initial_h_values (n=200), budget_s=600s\nInitialization:\n- Start with initial_h_values, scale to meet \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n- Initialize swarm: particles = [initial_h_values + random noise] with 30-50 particles\n- For each particle, clip and rescale to meet constraints\n\nPSO loop:\nFor t in 1..max_iter:\n   For each particle:\n      1. Update velocity: v = \u03c9*v + \u03b1*random()*(pbest - current) + \u03b2*random()*(gbest - current)\n      2. Update position: h = current + v\n      3. Clip h to [0,1] and rescale to \u2211h = n_points / 2\n      4. Compute objective C\u2085 using np.correlate\n      5. Update personal best if current is better\n   Update global best from all pbest\n   Track best solution found so far\n\nRefinement phase:\nAfter PSO completes, apply L-BFGS-B optimization to the best particle with:\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n- Objective function: same as above\n\nTermination:\nIf time budget expires, return the best solution found. If refinement fails, fallback to PSO's best.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- 40 particles for swarm\n- \u03c9=0.8, \u03b1=1.5, \u03b2=1.5\n- max_iter=200\n- Random noise amplitude: \u00b10.05\n\nVariations:\n- If stagnation detected (no improvement for 50 iterations): \n   - Reduce \u03c9 to 0.4 for increased exploration\n   - Increase \u03b1 to 2.5 to emphasize cognitive component\n- When \u2211h[i] deviates >1e-5 from target: \n   - Apply forced rescaling (h = h * (target / \u2211h))\n- If PSO fails to converge within time:\n   - Switch to gradient-based optimization with SLSQP\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime estimation:\n- PSO iterations: 200 * 40 * 200 operations \u2192 1.6 million\n- Refinement: 50 * 200 operations \u2192 10,000 \nTotal estimate: 1.61 million operations @ 100 operations/sec \u2192 16,100 sec (too slow)\n\nOptimized schedule:\n- Start with 40 particles and 200 max_iter\n- After 150s, switch to 20 particles and 300 max_iter\n- After 250s, apply L-BFGS-B with 50 iterations\n- Check objective every 20 iterations to save best\n\nRobustness measures:\n- Clip all h[i] to [0,1] after each update\n- Rescale to meet \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2 using h = h * (target / \u2211h)\n- If objective becomes NaN/inf, revert to last valid solution\n- If local optimizer fails, return PSO's best\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFeasibility checks:\n- All h[i] must be in [0, 1] (enforced by clipping)\n- \u2211h[i] must equal n_points / 2 (enforced by rescaling)\n- Objective must be finite (NaN/inf are invalid)\n\nValidation steps:\n1. Re-calculate C\u2085 using np.correlate and verify it matches the objective\n2. Check that \u2211h[i] * dx \u2248 1 within 1e-6 tolerance\n3. Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0, 1] with absolute tolerance 1e-6\n4. If any check fails, return the last valid solution\n\nReturn format:\n(h_values.tolist(), validated_c5_bound, n_points)\n\nSanity checks:\n- If c5_bound > 0.381835, log warning and return parent\n- If final h_values has all h[i] = 0.5, return parent\n- If PSO gets stuck in same solution for 3 iterations, apply small random perturbation",
